{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/189235-tremere-mage-sin-eaters","id":189235,"title":"Tremere (mage) Sin-Eaters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-06T00:54:39-07:00","id":189235,"title":"Tremere (mage) Sin-Eaters?","content":"Has anyone tried remaking Tremere as a krewe, rather than a Legacy? How did that work out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1738-charon","name":"Charon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T04:09:54-07:00","id":189306,"title":"","content":"While it would certainly be possible to create something that effectively works the same as the Tremere, downright recreating the Tremere as Sin-Eater Krewe who must steal the souls of people in order to sustain themselves, kinda uses Krewe's for something they're not. A Krewe is a mish mash of religion and ideology all come together to form a cohesive whole. Where a Legacy is a Mage transforming a his soul into what he percieves as something closer to a supernal truth, a Krewe is less of a gambit for power and more of a clueless groping after a glimmer of truth.<br /> I'de say it is far from impossible to recreate the Tremere as a group of Sin-Eaters. Sounds pretty interesting in fact. But to do it as a Krewe, is wrong in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T10:52:08-07:00","id":233028,"title":"","content":"Krewes, frankly, feel more at home in Mage anyway. Sin-eaters shouldn't concern themselves with a higher truth. That not only doesn't fit them, but it outright contradicts the strong themes of syncretism that are present throughout the book when Sin-eaters create a stable ideology and set themselves up as Gods. If anything, though, doing Tremere as a Krewe seems perfectly fine with how they're presented in Mage.<br /> <br /> Of course, unless they're a Krewe who were the slaves of a vampire, the backstory doesn't really work. But &quot;we eat souls because it will open the TRUTH&quot; is fitting with Krewes as they exist now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:40:41-07:00","id":233081,"title":"","content":"Krewes generate a focused course of action that pushes against the rudderless Brownian motion of the post-Bargain &quot;I don't even know what to believe anymore&quot; and the fixed loops that characterize death-as-portrayed-by-ghosts that is the Bound's primary stated reason for not being too attached to tradition. It gives the characters a light at the end of the tunnel to direct themselves by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:28:58-07:00","id":233567,"title":"","content":"I feel like you and I are frankly never going to agree on the Krewes, but I'm sorry, that's just a load of crap.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:03:47-07:00","id":234910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/189235-tremere-mage-sin-eaters?p=233028#post233028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Krewes, frankly, feel more at home in Mage anyway. Sin-eaters shouldn't concern themselves with a higher truth. That not only doesn't fit them, but it outright contradicts the strong themes of syncretism that are present throughout the book when Sin-eaters create a stable ideology and set themselves up as Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Syncretic ideologies are often built around a few central tenants which seldom change while the rest is prone to being replaced if it proves unsuitable, which is why the amorphous hodge-podge of European occult thought has a number of surprisingly consistent ideas. Also why wouldn't Sin Eaters set themselves up as Gods? That the geists are the little gods of death is one of the objective truths of their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T07:42:06-07:00","id":235397,"title":"","content":"What I mean is that you go from the champloo style &quot;clap your hands if you believe&quot; style of syncretism for the ceremonies and strengthening Resonance of a haunt to something defined and &quot;real&quot; for the Krewe Channel. It doesn't fit together. Throughout the rest of Sin-eater culture as it's presented, you have this notion that the trappings aren't important so much as the belief behind it, or at least the fact that <i>something</i> is being done. For the Channel on the other hand, it becomes a hard and fast <i>thing</i> that the Sin-eaters accept or reject, but never really disbelieve. I've said before that it feels like the only Sin-eaters who'd buy into the Channels and believe theirs has any merit (while likewise believing that everyone else's is a lie) are the Sacrosanct.<br /> <br /> That said, talk of what krewes mean is veering off a little, and I don't like taking over people's threads. Might be better suited <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book\">for here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}